# _identity.env — UPSTREAM-IDENTITY reverse map for the admin-bff-api Tier-1 overlay.
#
# These are the ORIGINAL literal values that the 3 brand-coupled tokens carry in
# the READ-ONLY upstream base (snapdragon-admin-bff-api @ Snapdragon-Systems). They
# are NOT secrets and NOT tenant brand — they are the base's own identity.
#
# scripts/validate-repo-templates.sh renders the overlay with EXACTLY these values
# and asserts the result is byte-identical to a freshly-pulled base. If the base
# drifts in any overlaid file (a non-templated line changed, or a templated line's
# surrounding context moved), that byte-compare breaks and the validator fails
# loudly (patch-reject + overlayed-region checksum). This is how the overlay stays
# honest without ever vendoring the base into the generator.
#
# NOT consumed by the renderer at emit time — render_repo_tree.sh derives the REAL
# tenant values from the brand profile. This file is the drift oracle only.
#
# Shell-sourced KEY=VALUE (same idiom as brands/*.conf and login-ui/_identity.env).
#
# CLUSTER_DOMAIN — the 4 app.yml env-DEFAULT seams (issuer-uri, jwk-set-uri nested
#   issuer, app.admin-emails, app.appstore.builder.registry) resolve to id./registry./
#   admin@ under this domain. Upstream literal: snapdragon.systems.
CLUSTER_DOMAIN="snapdragon.systems"
# BRAND_TITLE — the app.mfa.totp.issuer default (the otpauth/authenticator display
#   brand + WebAuthn RP name). Upstream literal: Snapdragon.
BRAND_TITLE="Snapdragon"
# GENERATOR_ORG_GROUP — the .gitlab-ci.yml `include:` project org/group. The
#   '/snapdragon-generator' path segment + the pentest file path stay literal (upstream
#   code identity); only the org/group is rebranded. Upstream literal below.
GENERATOR_ORG_GROUP="Snapdragon-Systems/snapdragon-generator"
